      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/28/flavio-bolsonaro-miami-us-fleeing-brazilian-election-defeat",
      "description": "<p>Far-right senator and family land in US after crossing from Brazil into Argentina and then flying via Ecuador</p><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/fl-vio-bolsonaro\">Flávio Bolsonaro</a> declared himself the “true president” of <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/brazil\">Brazil</a> after losing last Sunday’s presidential election and fleeing to the United States.</p><p>After landing on a private jet with his family in Miami, <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/florida\">Florida</a>, on Wednesday morning, the far-right senator published the claim in a letter – even though his own party has recognised the legitimate victory of <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/luiz-inacio-lula-da-silva\">Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva</a>, as have all of Brazil’s institutions, and international observers who monitored and endorsed the vote.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/28/flavio-bolsonaro-miami-us-fleeing-brazilian-election-defeat\">Continue reading...</a>",
